@startuml
title BO — manage staff availability (schedule, breaks, time-off)

actor Staff
participant "NGINX" as NGINX
participant "FE (Next.js BO)" as FE
participant "BE (Django/DRF)" as BE
database "DB (PostgreSQL)" as DB

' All endpoints below are gated by IsStaffMember (role staff/admin).
' Bookable slots are GENERATED DYNAMICALLY from this data (database.md) —
' nothing here is stored as a fixed slot.

== Read the weekly schedule ==
Staff -> FE : open Availability
FE -> NGINX : GET /bo/v1/availability/staff/{staffId}/schedule/  (Cookie: sessionid)
NGINX -> BE : proxy
note over BE
  availability.views.BoStaffScheduleView.get (IsStaffMember)
  availability.selectors.list_schedules()
end note
BE -> DB : SELECT availability_staffschedule
BE --> FE : 200 (StaffScheduleSerializer[])

== Replace the whole weekly schedule ==
Staff -> FE : edit weekly hours, save
FE -> NGINX : PUT /bo/v1/availability/staff/{staffId}/schedule/  (X-CSRFToken)
NGINX -> BE : proxy
note over BE
  availability.serializers.WeeklyScheduleWriteSerializer.is_valid()
end note
BE -> BE : availability.services.replace_weekly_schedule()
note over BE
  PUT REPLACES the entire weekly schedule (delete all + recreate),
  inside a transaction. Per entry:
  - weekday in 1..7  (1=Sun .. 7=Sat — clinic convention, database.md)
  - end_time after start_time (_validate_window)
end note
BE -> DB : DELETE then INSERT availability_staffschedule (atomic)
BE --> FE : 200 (StaffScheduleSerializer[])

== Daily break windows (e.g. lunch) ==
Staff -> FE : add a break
FE -> NGINX : POST /bo/v1/availability/staff/{staffId}/breaks/  (X-CSRFToken)
NGINX -> BE : proxy
BE -> BE : availability.services.add_break()
note over BE
  weekday 1..7; end_time after start_time. Break windows are
  non-bookable and subtracted during slot generation (business-rules.md).
end note
BE -> DB : INSERT availability_staffbreak
BE --> FE : 201 (StaffBreakSerializer)

Staff -> FE : remove a break
FE -> NGINX : DELETE /bo/v1/availability/staff/{staffId}/breaks/{breakId}/
NGINX -> BE : proxy
BE -> BE : availability.services.delete_break()
BE -> DB : DELETE availability_staffbreak
BE --> FE : 204 No Content

== Time-off / holidays (date ranges) ==
Staff -> FE : block time off
FE -> NGINX : POST /bo/v1/availability/staff/{staffId}/time-off/  (X-CSRFToken)
NGINX -> BE : proxy
BE -> BE : availability.services.add_time_off()
note over BE
  end_at must be after start_at. Time-off is stored as a UTC
  TIMESTAMPTZ range and removes that availability during slot generation.
end note
BE -> DB : INSERT availability_stafftimeoff
BE --> FE : 201 (StaffTimeOffSerializer)

Staff -> FE : remove time off
FE -> NGINX : DELETE /bo/v1/availability/staff/{staffId}/time-off/{timeOffId}/
NGINX -> BE : proxy
BE -> BE : availability.services.delete_time_off()
BE -> DB : DELETE availability_stafftimeoff
BE --> FE : 204 No Content

note over Staff, DB
  Clients never see this data directly: GET /v1/availability/slots
  calls availability.services.generate_slots(), which derives bookable
  start times from schedule minus breaks, time-off, and existing
  appointments — slots are NEVER persisted (database.md).
end note
@enduml
